Decisions Made
- Restored the peer-review workflow as reviewing-with-peer-agents.
- Kept review delegation tool- and command-neutral at skill level.
- Pass work intent and an observable decision record to reviewers.
- Route verified findings through bounded autofixing, except explicit review-only requests.

Problems Encountered
- The system Ruby 2.6 lacked Array#filter_map; mise x selected Ruby 4.0.6 for the full deterministic suite.

Constraints Identified
- Reviewers remain read-only and may not mutate external state.
- Autofixing stays inside the established review boundary and never grants commit, push, or comment capability.
- Model-backed evals, when used, must be scoped and token-efficient.

Open Questions
- None.

Context
- Added three functional eval paths, generated trigger coverage, global mutation-safety checks, inventory updates, and dedicated regression tests.
- Full deterministic suite and 211-case eval validation passed before shipping.
